Track 3: The After-Migration Gala
- Story & Context: In the ruins of the abandoned processing plant, the community now gathers to celebrate the anniversary of their first ascent, drumming on the very pipes that once dictated their confinement. The legend of the "Pipe-King" is whispered among the youth, claiming that if you press your ear to the ground, you can hear the vibration of the original rhythm still echoing through the crust. "We dance because the earth gave us the beat back," they chant in unison, turning the site of their struggle into a temple of rhythmic liberation.
